    "reason": "The release note [ev-25015016b295] and the PR [ev-a659463a22b9] only say that Kubernetes 1.32 is now the minimum supported version, and the compatibility row [ev-f88a947c0d4c] only lists \">= 1.32.0\". None of them says that installing or upgrading on an older cluster fails, so upgrade-blocked (critical) goes beyond the evidence. The PR changes cmd/flux/check.go and the check_pre golden file [ev-2efbf3d58fc9], which suggests the `flux check --pre` version check was updated. It does not show whether that check only reports a problem or stops install, bootstrap or upgrade, and the upgrade guide excerpt [ev-b1e8ad65539c] doesn't say either. To settle the consequence we need the check.go diff, or upstream text saying what happens on clusters older than 1.32.",
